Unclear. Supplied wording does not establish incorporation, applicability or performance in a particular contract; complete first paragraph excerpt: “2. Service Credits. If Acme Cloud does not meet the Service Commitment, Customer will be eligible to receive a Service Credit as a percentage of the monthly fees paid for the affected month, as follows:
(a) Monthly Uptime Percentage less than 99.99% but equal to or greater than 99.0%: 10% Service Credit;
(b) Monthly Uptime Percentage less than 99.0% but equal to or greater than 95.0%: 25% Service Credit;
(c) Monthly Uptime Percentage less than 95.0%: 50% Service Credit.”; time-bearing candidate paragraph 7: “3. Claims. To receive a Service Credit, Customer must submit a claim to support within thirty (30) days after the end of the month in which the downtime occurred. Service Credits are Customer's sole remedy.”; time-bearing candidate paragraph 8: “4. Exclusions. The Service Commitment does not apply to scheduled maintenance announced at least 48 hours in advance or to degraded performance that does not make the Platform unavailable.”; time-bearing candidate paragraph 2: “1. Service Commitment. Acme Cloud will use commercially reasonable efforts to make the Platform available with a Monthly Uptime Percentage of at least 99.99% during each calendar month (the "Service Commitment").”; remaining context is retained in clauses.
